==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|biðja}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*bidjaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|bitten}}, {{cog|fo|biðja}}, {{cog|da|bede}}, {{cog|sv|bedja}}, English [[bid]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈpɪðja/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɪðja|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|bað|báðu|beðið}}

# {{lb|is|ambitransitive|governs the accusative|optionally ditransitive with genitive}} to [[ask]], [[request]] some action of someone
#: ''Ég '''bað''' þig nú bara um [[greiði|greiða]].''
#:: I just '''asked''' you a [[favour]].
# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[pray]]
#: ''Ég '''bið''' til [[Guð]]s.''
#:: I '''pray''' to [[God]].

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-s5|b|i|ð|j=j}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|ask}} {{l|is|beiðast}}

