==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*bidjaną||to ask for, request}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|biddan}}, {{cog|ofs|bidda}}, {{cog|osx|biddian}}, {{cog|goh|bitten}}, {{cog|got|𐌱𐌹𐌳𐌾𐌰𐌽}}. Ultimately from {{der|non|ine-pro|*gʷʰedʰ-||to request, pray, ask for}}.

===Alternative forms===

; Runic
* {{alter|non|ᛒᛁᚦᛁᛅ||infinitive}}
* {{alter|non|ᛒᛅᚦ||first/third singular past indicative}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|12th century Icelandic}} {{IPA|non|/ˈbiðjɑ/}}

===Verb===
{{non-verb|bað|báðu|beðinn}}

# to [[ask]], [[beg]], [[request]]
#* ''[[w:Völuspá|Vǫluspá]]'', verse 1, lines 1-2, in '''1860''', T. Möbius, ''Edda Sæmundar hins fróða: mit einem Anhang zum Theil bisher ungedruckter Gedichte''. Leipzig, page [https://archive.org/stream/eddasmundarhins00mbgoog#page/n22 1]:
#*: Hljóðs '''bið''' ek allar / helgar kindir, {{...}}
#*: ''For silence I '''ask''' ''/'' all holy kindreds'' {{...}}
# to [[pray]]
#* ''Saga Ólafs konúngs Tryggvasonar'' 279, in '''1827''', [[w:Sveinbjörn_Egilsson|S. Egilsson]], Þ. Guðmundsson, ''Fornmanna sögur'', Volume III. Copenhagen, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=BFRSAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA48 48]:
#*: {{...}} hann vakti laungum um nóttum ok '''bað''' til guðs góðgjarnliga fur vinum. {{...}}
#*: {{...}} ''many times he rose in the night and '''prayed''' to the merciful God for [his] friends.'' {{...}}

